DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(e^((x^2+3*x+2)))^4");
$fun_1 = Formula("(x*4)^2-4*((x)^(1/3))+1");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((((1, 12) U {-10, -7, -5, 0, 1, 6} U {-9, -4, 9})) - (((1, 12))))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-10, -7, -5, 0, 1, 6} U ({-10, -7, -5, 0, 1, 6}) U {-9, -4, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (1, 12))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("((1, 12) - (1, 12))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(3, 10) U [4, 10] U [4, 10] U [4, 10]");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((3, 10)) U [4, 10]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`10+13+5/8`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(23.625),width=>9}
---

[`9+14-19+9/4`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(6.25),width=>3}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 \leq x \leq 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 < x < 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -7, -5, 0, 1, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 < x < 12\}`]
- [`C = \{-9, -4, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B \cup A \cup C)) - ((B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup (A) \cup C \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, -3, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 10, -2, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -2, 10, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-2, 10, 2>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -3, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -3, 2>") . Compute("<10, -2, 8>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 10, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, -2, 8>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, -3, 5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, -9, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -3, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -3, 5>") x Compute("<-5, -9, 8>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -3, 5>") . Compute("<-5, -9, 8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, -3, 5>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -9, 8>") x Compute("<3, -3, 5>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, -9, 8>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
